    <h2>Getting Your British Canoeing SUP License</h2>
    <p>
      UK River Access: Do I Need a License to Paddleboard on a River?
    </p>
    <p>
      The most common question we get from new paddlers is: "do i need a license to paddleboard on a river?" The short answer is yes, for the vast majority of inland waterways in the UK, you are legally required to hold a waterways license.
    </p>
    <p>
      Navigating the legalities of UK rivers can be confusing. Below, we break down exactly what licenses you need, where to get them, and the unwritten rules of the river.
    </p>
    <p>
      The most cost-effective and comprehensive way to ensure you are paddling legally is to obtain a british canoeing sup license (now managed under Paddle UK). Becoming a member automatically grants you a waterways license that covers over 4,500km of managed rivers and canals, including those maintained by the Canal &amp; River Trust and the Environment Agency. [Source: Paddle UK / British Canoeing]
    </p>
    <p>
      Without this license, you risk being fined by waterway enforcement officers. The fee also directly contributes to maintaining launch points and clearing invasive species from the rivers.
    </p>
